<section style="padding: 72px 24px;"><div style="max-width: 1000px; margin: 0px auto; display: flex; flex-direction: column; align-items: center; gap: 24px; text-align: center;"><h2 style="margin: 0px; font-size: 23px; line-height: 32.2px; font-weight: 400;">Born in the Salon. Rooted in Nature.</h2><p style="margin: 0px; font-size: 16px; line-height: 22.4px;">AMUN was founded by Sophia Tullio, daughter of renowned precision hairstylist Michael Tullio, whose legacy spans over 30 years at Salon Tullio in Aspen, Colorado.</p><p style="margin: 0px; font-size: 16px; line-height: 22.4px;">Raised in the world of luxury hair care, Sophia understood the artistry, precision, and uncompromising performance demanded by the industry’s finest professional products. But after navigating years of debilitating health challenges, her passion for healing and research into conventional beauty formulations revealed a troubling disconnect between the products we use to look beautiful and the ingredients we expose our bodies to.</p><p style="margin: 0px; font-size: 16px; line-height: 22.4px;">AMUN was created to bridge two worlds that she believes should never be separate: professional luxury performance and uncompromising personal well-being.</p><p style="margin: 0px; font-size: 16px; line-height: 22.4px;">Every formula was custom-developed to meet the demands of professional stylists, combining carefully selected botanicals, grass-fed tallow sourced with regenerative principles, and organic ingredients wherever possible, without sacrificing results.</p><p style="margin: 0px; font-size: 16px; line-height: 22.4px;">Today, AMUN is used by the stylists at Salon Tullio across diverse hair types, bringing ancestral ingredients into the hands of modern hair professionals.</p><p style="margin: 6px 0 0; font-family: 'Sentient', Georgia, serif; font-size: 18px; line-height: 25.2px; font-style: italic;">Born from professional expertise. Driven by a pursuit of health. Created to prove that nature and performance belong together.</p></div></section>
